Near miss for mismatched_block_end: a :WHILE holding an :IF that lost its
:ENDIF, then the :ENDWHILE. A matching opener sits deeper in the stack,
so the scanner recovers: the :IF is unclosed_block and the :ENDWHILE
closes the loop. mismatched_block_end must NOT fire (catalog fence,
commit be7a174).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CountDown;
	:PARAMETERS nStart;
	:DECLARE nCurrent;
	nCurrent := nStart;
	:WHILE nCurrent > 0;
		:IF nCurrent % 2 == 0;
			nCurrent := nCurrent - 2;
	:ENDWHILE;
	:RETURN nCurrent;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CountDown;
	:PARAMETERS nStart;
	:DECLARE nCurrent;
	nCurrent := nStart;
	:WHILE nCurrent > 0;
		:IF nCurrent % 2 == 0;
			nCurrent := nCurrent - 2;
		:ENDWHILE;
		:RETURN nCurrent;
	:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:3-6:6 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:3-6:6 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
